  "scope": [
    "Both mode-aware service entry points now use MessageApplication. The retained normal-local C2S path reaches the existing standalone or clustered archive transaction with an operation-bound direct witness.",
    "The actual COMMIT wrapper records unconfirmed preparation before polling COMMIT and a positive receipt synchronously before health-turn completion or result mapping. Stored, Replay and AccountUnavailable remain distinct from returned route mode.",
    "One private original-message preparation derives admission, identity, live, stored and complete policy-selected archive views. It preserves full/bare and delayed/live differences, self-recipient behavior and un-rated durable messages without inventing a guard grant.",
    "Positive Stored receipt followed by continuation error preserves accepted recovery storage; Replay performs the existing no-route finalization; AccountUnavailable preserves rejection. No reconciliation read or second admission is introduced.",
    "Reverse-order begin/finalize/direct transitions, changed prepared inputs, duplicate effect use and invalid LiveOnly admission mode reject without changing retained facts."
  ],
